            claim: "\"Form an LLC to protect your personal assets.\" Formation is presented as the moment protection begins.",
            problem: "Filing creates the entity; it does not by itself create a reliable shield. The protection depends on conduct afterwards, and the most common way small companies lose it is mundane: paying personal expenses from the business account and business expenses from the personal one. Commingling funds is the fact pattern most often cited when a court disregards the entity, and it is also the thing a founder does casually in month one because the shield feels like a completed purchase. Two further conditions get omitted \u2014 a governing document, which is what evidences that a single-member entity is genuinely separate from its owner, and the reality that a personal guarantee on a lease or loan, and personal liability for your own negligent acts, sit outside the shield entirely no matter how well maintained it is.",
