            problem: "Both are answers to the wrong question. The decision is not general; it is per task, and the correct split is stable enough to publish. Formation filings, EIN, agent selection and adopting a contract template you have read are genuinely fine to self-serve \u2014 and paying a service for an EIN, which the IRS issues free in minutes, is pure waste. But founder equity splits, anything involving investors, employment terminations, a received demand letter and enterprise contracts with uncapped liability are all cases where the cost of the mistake exceeds any plausible fee by orders of magnitude. Generic advice in either direction produces a predictable error: over-spending on the commodity filings, then economising on the equity split, which is the single most expensive thing a small company can get wrong.",
